  "tuning_disclosure": {
    "rusteda": "The RustEDA arm is the qualified opt-in IHP profile chosen after the recorded IHP trials on the benchmark page (reset-specialized and arbitrary-initial-state aligned selects, path-aware pin access, optional via reduction on and off). Its tuning targeted power, area and setup Fmax at the shared gates, not LibreLane's runtime.",
    "librelane": "The published LibreLane recipe was tuned for closure on IHP (antenna margin 50, 6/4 repair iterations, cell and diode padding, post-GRT resizer margins 1.0/0.2 ns with full TNS repair). This plan screens it against two arms that restore LibreLane defaults for the antenna and resizer knobs, under the same selection rule and the same gates. Geometry, routing layers, padding, CTS and floorplan knobs stay as published. An amendment added a fourth arm, jumper-only antenna repair after detailed routing, once the first screening sample showed that diode loads cause LibreLane's timing-gate rows; it can only help LibreLane."
  },
